WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.850
By day, this person holds the door for
strangers and picks up litter that isn't

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.020
theirs.

3
00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:10.810
One night, they pull up their
hood and join a huge, noisy crowd.

4
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:16.310
The crowd surges towards a shop window,
and their arm goes up with everyone else's.

5
00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.770
Alone, they would never do this.

6
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.550
So what has the crowd changed?

7
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.950
In this mission, you'll see
that crowds can be anti-social,

8
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.040
harming people or property, but
also pro-social, helping others.

9
00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:34.290
You'll explore what happens when
nobody around you can tell who you are.

10
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:38.550
And you'll ask why some people
don't get swept along at all.

11
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.580
Your mission: explain why polite people
do things in a crowd that they would never

12
00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:44.510
do alone.
